{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgz4bJfzHHvKgjbQWUVqm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1. **What I'm meant to do next:** I don't know. My last action was checking the journal after handing the book to Never-Sold, and I never read what it said. If nothing is active, the job is probably finished. If something new appeared, it most likely follows from the Broker, Ussa-Rekh, or from the eleven at Thorn, since those are the loose ends I left.\n\n2. **Who I work for:** Never-Sold and the Chainbreakers. She named me one of them and has paid me for each job. I work for her because she pays, and because I believe in freeing people from Owings. I'm less sure of her methods, and she seems to be as well. She said we'd be called \"the people who loose killers\" and that it would be true.\n\n3. **Most confusing moment:** The Broker's tokens. I couldn't tell whether Ussa-Rekh was a villain or a man holding the crew's debt for reasons that made sense to him. Also, my Speech was too low for the peaceful options, so I ended up paying Feldril Nethri and stealing from the Broker's house. I then didn't know whether the game wanted that, or whether I'd skipped the better route. Many lines also showed up as placeholder \"gist\" text, which made it harder to follow people's motives.\n\n4. **What I'd tell the writer:** The moral weight is strong. Killing to free people, and a rescue that costs someone else, both land well. Please tell the player earlier when a skill check will lock out a route, and give a non-theft way through. Write out the placeholder lines. Show me what happens to the eleven at Thorn, and what the Broker was to Never-Sold. I want to see the consequences of what I chose."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3542,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_